{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538458981,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNjU3NDg3ODI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2889","origin":"github"},"title":"Simplify path annotation","message":"With the low-level Git/annex query support growing in #2882 the monster that is path annotation can now be tamed. The problem is that it is an incomprehensible beast that aims to be clever by figuring out the nature of particular paths without asking Git. That makes it fast and fragile at the same time.\n\nPath annotation should be RF'ed to rely on the `*status()` and `get_content_*info()` reports in the base classes and only retain select functionality for exploring dataset hierarchies and untracked directory tree.\n\nI am hopeful that min. 50% of the code can be deleted without much (if any) loss in speed.","files":null}]}